rgin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":0.032031381540404594,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":16.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5393941024662711,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":10.1,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.05814082592720284,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.017089226353049762,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":27.6,"_gate_pool_share":-0.23146383912594293,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03008844920453324,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":40.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.1302397859386728,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":90.1,"_gate_margins":0.010783185488717938,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":60.8,"_gate_fund_growth":0.10417938336089645,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.049725431049796445,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":66.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.05519563637494507,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006814393567996862,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.00863,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.778,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":77.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"Aptiv PLC, an industrial technology company, provides hardware and software solutions to support automotive and other industries in North America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and South America. It operates through three segments: Advanced Safety and User Experience, Engineered Components, and Electrical Distribution Systems. The company offers active safety, user experience and smart vehicle compute, and software products for vehicle safety and security, including intelligent sensors, compute platforms, and software tools and services. It also provides connection systems, interconnects, and cable management and protection solutions for the distribution of power, signal, and data. Aptiv PLC was incorporated in 2011 and is based in Schaffhausen, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin P. Clark | Chairman, CEO & President of Intelligent Systems | Age 63 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 140K people. Revenue per employee of $146K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $993 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 28\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Aptiv PLC is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.0B market cap on $20.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 7% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 13.24\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -8.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 74% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 63% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Insiders are net buyers (78% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $8.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Research Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for November 6th (ABNB, ADNT, ALL, AMC, AMPL, APTV, BDX, BROS, CAVA, ET)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/research-analysts-price-target-changes-for-november-6th-abnb-adnt-all-amc-ampl-aptv-bdx-bros-cava-et.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794007006.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Aptiv (NYSE:APTV) Stock Price Target Lowered at Citigroup","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/aptiv-nyseaptv-stock-price-target-lowered-at-citigroup.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003169.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Can Aptiv PLC (NYSE:APTV) Turn Its Technology Push Into Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/can-aptiv-plc-nyseaptv-turn-its-technology-push-into-growth","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793826780.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.452,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Is Aptiv (APTV) Signaling With $13 Billion In New Business Awards?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-aptv/aptiv/news/what-is-aptiv-aptv-signaling-with-13-billion-in-new-business","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793788109.776,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Aptiv (APTV) Faces A Fair Value Test On Mixed Third Quarter Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aptiv-aptv-faces-fair-value-101923845.html","date":"2026-11-04","t